{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"740291949843447869","content":"Web and Baeshra finish the short trek to <#739055783806894110>","created_at":"2020-08-07T10:51:02.145000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"741247023663284236","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Sketchy Bee 🐝","id":"297577343554158603","is_bot":0,"username":"sketchybee"},"author_id":"297577343554158603","channel_id":"740291949843447869","content":"As soon as they're gone, Leaf climbs up into the tree to the highest branch she can safely sit on. Once there, she pulls out the note Copper left about room 15 and waiting an hour. An hour... that's all it was. In such a short time, she'd managed to break in two. She looks down at it, thinking about how it revealed parts of herself she thought she'd long oppressed. Leaf holds the paper out in front of her. With all the lies and secrets surrounding this paper and it's appearance on her pillow in room 7, Leaf resolves to hold onto truth. In Goblin she says confidently, ||\"My name is Leaf. I am a called goblin of the Wild Mother and best friend to Mello. No lies or secret plots can take that away, and nothing I ever do will change that truth.\"|| She rips the paper in two and lets go, watching it drift off into the wind.","created_at":"2020-08-07T11:15:18.040000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"741253130129506404","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Sketchy Bee 🐝","id":"297577343554158603","is_bot":0,"username":"sketchybee"},"author_id":"297577343554158603","channel_id":"740291949843447869","content":"Leaf wakes up feeling much better than she did the morning before. She quietly climbs up to her small sanctuary for Mello and sits on the branch. Leaf places her holy symbol in her lap, thoughtfully looking over the wooden medallion. Her hands run over the carved symbol she never carved, and then flip to the flat, empty back. She takes out her bottle of ink and dips her pen in, carefully tracing it over the wood in the curving shape of a koi fish.","created_at":"2020-08-07T19:06:48.383000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"741371788428181637","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
